 sons of Joseph. He and his brother Ephraim were afterwards adopted by Jacob as his own sons (48:1).","verses":109,"father":"Joseph","mother":"Asenath","v":[1]},{"id":"machir_1877","name":"Machir","also":"Machirites","summary":"Manasseh’s oldest son (Josh. 17:1), or probably his only son (see 1 Chr. 7:14, 15; comp. Num. 26:29-33; Josh. 13:31). His descendants are referred to under the name of Machirites, being the offspring of Gilead (Num. 26:29).","verses":17,"father":"Manasseh","mother":"Concubine the Aramitess","v":[1]},{"id":"gilead_1317","name":"Gilead","also":"","summary":"Son of Manasseh.","verses":11,"father":"Machir","mother":"","v":[1]},{"id":"zelophehad_3035","name":"Zelophehad","also":"","summary":"First-born, of the tribe of Manasseh, and of the family of Gilead; died in the wilderness. Having left no sons, his daughters, concerned lest their father’s name should be “done away from among his family,” made an appeal to Moses, who, by divine direction, appointed it as “a statute of judgment” in Israel that daughters should inherit their father’s portion when no sons were left (Num. 27:1-11).","verses":9,"father":"Hepher","mother":"","v":[1,7]},{"id":"hepher_1496","name":"Hepher","also":"","summary":"The youngest son of Gilead (Num. 26:32; 27:1).","verses":5,"father":"Gilead","mother":"","v":[1]},{"id":"tirzah_2868","name":"Tirzah","also":"","summary":"The youngest of Zelophehad’s five daughters (Num. 26:33; Josh. 17:3).","verses":5,"father":"Zelophehad","mother":"","v":[1]},{"id":"hoglah_1548","name":"Hoglah","also":"","summary":"Partridge, one of the daughters of Zelophehad the Gileadite, to whom portions were assigned by Moses (Num. 26:33; 27:1; 36:11).","verses":4,"father":"Zelophehad","mother":"","v":[1]},{"id":"mahlah_1895","name":"Mahlah","also":"","summary":"Disease, one of the five daughters of Zelophehad (Num. 27:1-11) who had their father’s inheritance, the law of inheritance having been altered in their favour.","verses":4,"father":"Zelophehad","mother":"","v":[1]},{"id":"milcah_2083","name":"Milcah","also":"","summary":"Belonged to clans of Menasseh.","verses":4,"father":"Zelophehad","mother":"","v":[1]},{"id":"noah_2211","name":"Noah","also":"","summary":"Rest, (Heb. Noah) the grandson of Methuselah (Gen. 5:25-29), who was for two hundred and fifty years contemporary with Adam, and the son of Lamech, who was about fifty years old at the time of Adam’s death.","verses":4,"father":"Zelophehad","mother":"","v":[1]},{"id":"moses_2108","name":"Moses","also":"","summary":"Drawn (or Egypt. mesu, “son;” hence Rameses, royal son). On the invitation of Pharaoh (Gen. 45:17-25), Jacob and his sons went down into Egypt.","verses":774,"father":"Amram","mother":"Jochebed","v":[2,5,6,11,12,15,18,22,23]},{"id":"eleazar_1062","name":"Eleazar","also":"","summary":"The third son of Aaron (Ex. 6:23). His wife, a daughter of Putiel, bore him Phinehas (Ex. 6:25). After the death of Nadab and Abihu (Lev. 10:12; Num. 3:4) he was appointed to the charge of the sanctuary (Num. 3:32).","verses":61,"father":"Aaron","mother":"Elisheba","v":[2,19,21,22]},{"id":"korah_1795","name":"Korah","also":"Core","summary":"A Levite, the son of Izhar, the brother of Amram, the father of Moses and Aaron (Ex. 6:21). The institution of the Aaronic priesthood and the Levitical service at Sinai was a great religious revolution.","verses":26,"father":"Izhar","mother":"","v":[3]},{"id":"israel_682","name":"Israel","also":"","summary":"One who follows on another’s heels; supplanter, (Gen. 25:26; 27:36; Hos. 12:2-4), the second born of the twin sons of Isaac by Rebekah. He was born probably at Lahai-roi, when his father was fifty-nine and Abraham one hundred and fifty-nine years old.","verses":1009,"father":"Isaac","mother":"Rebekah","v":[8,11,12,20,21]},{"id":"aaron_1","name":"Aaron","also":"","summary":"The eldest son of Amram and Jochebed, a daughter of Levi (Ex. 6:20). Some explain the name as meaning mountaineer, others mountain of strength, illuminator.","verses":331,"father":"Amram","mother":"Jochebed","v":[13]},{"id":"joshua_1727","name":"Joshua","also":"Jehoshua, Oshea, Jesus, Jeshua, Hoshea","summary":"Jehovah is his help, or Jehovah the Saviour. The son of Nun, of the tribe of Ephraim, the successor of Moses as the leader of Israel.","verses":189,"father":"Nun","mother":"","v":[18,22]},{"id":"nun_2214","name":"Nun","also":"Non","summary":"Beyond the fact that he was the father of Joshua nothing more is known of him (Ex. 33:11).","verses":30,"father":"Elishama","mother":"","v":[18]}],"places":[{"id":"abarim_2","name":"Abarim","kind":"Region","lat":31.76136,"lon":35.74615,"summary":"Regions beyond; i.e., on the east of Jordan, a mountain, or rather a mountain-chain, over against Jericho, to the east and south-east of the Dead Sea, in the land of Moab.","verses":5,"v":[12]},{"id":"kadesh_661","name":"Kadesh","kind":"Oasis","lat":30.64805,"lon":34.42261,"summary":"Holy, or Kadesh-Barnea, sacred desert of wandering, a place on the south-eastern border of Palestine, about 165 miles from Horeb. It lay in the “wilderness” or “desert of Zin” (Gen. 14:7; Num. 13:3-26; 14:29-33; 20:1; 27:14), on the border of Edom (20:16).","verses":15,"v":[14]},{"id":"meribah_782","name":"Meribah","kind":"Landmark (Spring)","lat":30.68771,"lon":34.4948,"summary":"Another fountain having a similar origin in the desert of Zin, near to Kadesh (Num. 27:14). The two places are mentioned together in Deut. 33:8.","verses":4,"v":[14]},{"id":"zin_1261","name":"Zin","kind":"Region","lat":30.68771,"lon":34.4948,"summary":"A low palm-tree, the south-eastern corner of the desert et-Tih, the wilderness of Paran, between the Gulf of Akabah and the head of the Wady Guraiyeh (Num. 13:21).","verses":7,"v":[14]}],"events":[],"traditions":[],"sources":["JFB","MHCC","Wesley"],"tags":{"bsb":[[1323,1323,1323,6765,6765,1121,2660,2660,1121,1121,1568,1568,1121,1121,4353,4353,1121,1121,4519,4519,4940,4940,4940,4940,4519,4519,1121,3130,3130,428,8034,8034,803